    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1038/nclimate3103",
    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Southern Hemisphere climate change",
    "problem": "Understanding the causes of recent climate trends in the high-latitude Southern Hemisphere is hampered by a short instrumental record, making it difficult to distinguish natural variability from forced change and to reconcile observations with incompatible climate model simulations.",
    "method": "To assess recent high-latitude Southern Hemisphere climate trends, this paper proposes an approach that synthesizes instrumental, satellite, and palaeoclimate data and compares these observations with climate model simulations to distinguish forced changes from natural variability.",
    "task": "The task is to assess whether recent observed trends in high-latitude Southern Hemisphere surface climate are unusual by comparing them against the context of palaeoclimate records and climate model simulations to distinguish natural variability from forced change.",
