            "target_entity_instance": "West Antarctic Ice Sheet",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The importance of the latter process is par- ticularly evident along the margin of the WAIS\u2074\u2077\u207b\u2074\u2079 and is associated with regional atmospheric circulation changes forced by teleconnec- tions from the tropics \u2074\u2078,\u2075\u2070.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Amundsen Sea Low",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Antarctic Peninsula",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Antarctic Peninsula warming has been related to intensification of the circumpolar westerlies in austral summer and autumn\u00b9\u00b3, to associ- ated deepening of the ASL, and to central tropical Pacific warming in austral autumn, winter and spring\u00b9\u00b9.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "central tropical Pacific warming",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Antarctic Peninsula",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Antarctic Peninsula warming has been related to intensification of the circumpolar westerlies in austral summer and autumn\u00b9\u00b3, to associ- ated deepening of the ASL, and to central tropical Pacific warming in austral autumn, winter and spring\u00b9\u00b9.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "1939-1942 El Ni\u00f1o event",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "West Antarctica",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "An analysis of more than 20 ice-core records from West Antarctica\u2076\u2075 concluded that the most recent decades were probably the warmest in the past 200 years, but with low confidence because of a similar-magnitude warming event during the 1940s associated with the major 1939\u20131942 El Ni\u00f1o event\u2077\u2070.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "iceberg calving events",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Mertz glacier",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "For example, near the Mertz glacier, sea-ice proxy records spanning the past 250 years depict large multi-decadal variations that are attributed to iceberg calving events and are comparable to, or larger than, the most recent 36-year or 100-year trends\u2077\u00b3 (Supplementary Fig. 3b,c).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Southern Annular Mode",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "southern South America",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Similarly, an annual average SAM index reconstruction based on a network of temperature-sensitive palaeoclimate records spanning Antarctica and southern South America indicates that the SAM is currently in its most positive state over at least the past 1,000 years\u00b9\u2078.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
